## Round 4: Web Research Fixes (5)

Based on official Unity UAAL + AR Foundation documentation:

| # | File | Fix | Source |
|---|------|-----|--------|
| 17 | [ProjectSettings.asset](file:///c:/Users/apurv/Desktop/AWS%20Proto/unity_project/ProjectSettings/ProjectSettings.asset) | **Disabled multithreaded rendering** (`m_MTRendering: 0`, `mobileMTRendering.Android: 0`) | ARCore docs: "Disable Multithreaded Rendering — not supported" |
| 18 | [ProjectSettings.asset](file:///c:/Users/apurv/Desktop/AWS%20Proto/unity_project/ProjectSettings/ProjectSettings.asset) | Added **camera usage description** for AR | Required for camera permission on Android 10+ |
| 19 | [ProjectSettings.asset](file:///c:/Users/apurv/Desktop/AWS%20Proto/unity_project/ProjectSettings/ProjectSettings.asset) | Set `activeInputHandler: 2` (Both old + new Input System) | Required for `com.unity.inputsystem` compatibility |
| 20 | [EditorBuildSettings.asset](file:///c:/Users/apurv/Desktop/AWS%20Proto/unity_project/ProjectSettings/EditorBuildSettings.asset) | **Created** — sets ARScene as default build scene | Required for Unity to include scene in AAR export |
| 21 | [AutoSnapEngine.cs](file:///c:/Users/apurv/Desktop/AWS%20Proto/unity_project/Assets/Scripts/SceneManipulation/AutoSnapEngine.cs) | Added **[ApplyAutoSnap()](file:///c:/Users/apurv/Desktop/AWS%20Proto/unity_project/Assets/Scripts/SceneManipulation/AutoSnapEngine.cs#50-79)** method | Was called by bridge but didn't exist |

> [!NOTE]
> Existing config already correct: `AndroidMinSdkVersion: 24` ✅, `AndroidTargetArchitectures: 255` (all) ✅, Graphics APIs set to OpenGLES3 with `m_Automatic: 0` (no Vulkan) ✅, `ScriptingBackend` uses IL2CPP by default ✅.

